<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dewas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dewas is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, below a hill with a shrine of the goddess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chamunda">Chamunda</a>. From the 1720s it was shared by two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> Puar states, Dewas Senior and Dewas Junior, whose rulers lived in separate palaces in the same town until 1948. It is now an industrial city close to Indore.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dewas.jpg" alt="Dewas" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Akashwk07 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sayaji-Dwar,_Dewas_(M.P.).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
